id: pm-swarm-shared-tracker
title: Coordinate parallel agents on a shared tracker without git
description: "Make tracker coordination primary and Git worktree lanes optional, with real concurrent-process acceptance."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-20T09:59:13.604Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T16:12:20.692Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: All eight commands have explicit no-git behavior; existing Git tests and unchanged release gates pass; packed no-git consumer and concurrent claims retain healthy history.
parent: pm-swarm-07o2
comments[33]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T09:59:21.844Z",codex-agent,"Design: detect workspace mode once without invoking Git on non-repository paths; settings bypasses repository detection. Reuse certified SDK readiness, deterministic selection and overlap rules. Shared lanes are claimed items, with SDK claim provenance for age and no branch/base fields. Hold a tracker-local SDK lease across selection, claim and terminal reaping. Shared status reports declared overlaps, explicitly omitting Git measurements; watch emits overlap changes without claim-age polling noise. Sync accepts explicit portable files and retains preview/apply semantics; land explains the Git requirement. Preserve existing Git behavior and ownership checks; release terminal claims only for the invoking principal, reporting foreign claims as refused."
  "2026-10-20T10:06:16.141Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: shared tracker uses the host-bound SDK client, certified readiness and a tracker-local 60-second bounded operation lease. Eight simultaneous CLI processes retained eight distinct claims in the first run. Source-loaded test extension metadata causes strict health extension warnings, while integrity/history checks pass; test health isolates extension discovery and packed acceptance separately verifies the managed tarball. Pinned host gap: some expected extension refusals return exit 1 with human diagnostics and exit 2 with JSON. No CLI/SDK changes or dependency bumps."
  "2026-10-20T10:07:34.038Z",codex-agent,"Correction after tracing refusal handling: asynchronous method rejections bypassed runCommand catch because it returned promises without awaiting them. This is a package dispatcher issue, not a proven host JSON/human gap. Await operations inside the existing expected-error boundary so refusals consistently preserve the intended exit 2 and full actionable message. Regression assertions cover strict overlap, missing explicit files and Git-only landing refusals."
  "2026-10-20T10:10:29.579Z",codex-agent,"Focused refusal regressions now pass 3/3 after awaiting dispatcher operations. Contention run: eight processes, eight distinct claims retained, nine JSONL histories parse cleanly, strict health (source-extension discovery disabled only for this unmanaged fixture) passes; contention elapsed 26462 ms under concurrent host load. Managed packed acceptance runs next-to-sync-to-status-to-terminal-reap under Node and native Bun with Git absent from PATH."
  "2026-10-20T10:12:29.261Z",codex-agent,"Packed tarball acceptance passed under both Node and native Bun: pm install ./package.tgz --project in a non-Git tracker, then next, sync --files --apply, status, terminal stale-claim reap, and full managed-extension pm health --strict-exit. Git was absent from PATH for the loop; total targeted acceptance elapsed 136738 ms. Initial coverage exposed that source-loaded CLI extension code is not fully attributed to authored TypeScript by c8; adding direct registered-handler SDK coverage with real trackers alongside process acceptance, without changing source inventory or thresholds."
  "2026-10-20T10:13:15.840Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs in an isolated source copy with the same pinned SDK and real trackers: restoring only runCommand to origin/main makes 9/9 no-git regressions fail (exit 1), including the matrix where all eight commands exit 2 with first line Error: Command failed and git rev-parse in the detail. Disabling only SharedTracker.sharedExclusive makes the eight-process test fail (exit 1) on an already-claimed race. Reverting only the age-independent watch comparison makes the watch regression fail (exit 1) with spurious lane_changed events. Current implementations retained; source-import tests require no dist rebuild."
  "2026-10-20T10:20:23.240Z",codex-agent,"Additional artifact revert proof: rebuilt an isolated source copy with only runCommand reverted to origin/main, packed it, installed the tarball in a real non-Git tracker, and ran the new packed acceptance. Build passed; acceptance failed at next with host exit 2 and test exit 1. This independently proves the compiled installed artifact test detects the original Git prerequisite."
  "2026-10-20T10:24:39.306Z",codex-agent,"Native human-output matrix passes: plan, next, start, status, sync with explicit files, reap and settings exit 0. Coordination results begin mode: shared-tracker; settings begins swarm:. Land deliberately exits 2 with the explicit branch-merge requirement in its detail; the host retains first-line title Error: Command failed. The old dispatcher proof exits 2 with that generic first line for every command. docs/shared-tracker-verification.md records exact before/after lines and the artifact revert proof."
  "2026-10-20T10:25:56.388Z",codex-agent,"Registered PM test run passed 14/14 regressions, zero failures/skips/cancellations: pm test pm-swarm-shared-tracker --run --progress --only-index 1 --timeout 600 --workspace-context source --override-linked-workspace-context --pm-context tracker --override-linked-pm-context. Contention elapsed 50093 ms; eight unique retained claims, nine valid histories and strict integrity/history health. Full coverage run: 110/111 pass, with one existing TOON watch deadline failure under host load; new shared-tracker source reaches all four 100 percent metrics. Serial release gates will rerun the unchanged watch test and full inventory."
  "2026-10-20T10:27:58.051Z",codex-agent,"Repository health boundary: the live package tracker reports pre-existing stale_in_progress_items:6 plus an ignored local pm-github extension host-version skew (pinned host 2026.10.15 versus extension host 2026.10.20). Integrity and history drift checks are clean. These are separate from passing non-Git fixture health and from release:check; no existing item histories or dependency pins were rewritten."
  "2026-10-20T10:45:19.030Z",codex-agent,"Final mode-detection refinement: Git ceilings stop ancestor discovery but do not suppress a worktree marker in the current directory. A real Git regression fails 0/1 with the initial repositoryRoot function and passes 1/1 after moving the ceiling check to the parent step; the existing non-Git parent-ceiling case still passes. Focused package test and typecheck pass. The preceding npm run reached 111/111 and four 100 percent coverage metrics (1504 statements/lines, 90 functions, 735 branches); both full gates will be rerun after this two-line correction."
  "2026-10-20T10:53:32.183Z",codex-agent,"Preserved the existing Git-mode refusal transport: the first asynchronous error-boundary change also changed Git failures from exit 1 to exit 2. A new real-Git regression fails with unconditional awaiting (exit 2 versus expected 1). Await only shared-mode operations; the Git refusal, current-directory ceiling and shared landing refusal regressions now pass 3/3. Typecheck, lint and zero-duplication gate pass. No existing Git test was edited."
  "2026-10-20T11:01:52.016Z",codex-agent,"CI on 5eef502 passed all 112 behavioral tests on Node 22 and Node 26 but measured one unfulfilled conditional-await branch in shared land, yielding 99.86 percent branches. Put the Git-only refusal directly in the dispatcher's mode guard and reuse the same public-safe message in the embedded engine. Focused landing, ceiling and unchanged Git refusal tests pass 3/3; types, lint, docstrings and zero duplication pass. No coverage threshold, inventory or exclusion changed. Stopped the redundant local run after this actionable CI failure; full final gates restart on the corrected source."
  "2026-10-20T11:27:39.741Z",codex-agent,"Final npm run release:check passed on source commit 7a59afa with isolated HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 and CI=1 under nvm Node 26.12.0. Suite 112/112 and packed acceptance 3/3 pass, zero failures/skips/cancellations. All 24 authored files retain 100 percent statements/lines (1523/1523), functions (90/90) and branches (753/753); zero duplication, types, lint, docstrings, production audit, package allowlist, changelog and attestation pass. Eight processes retained eight unique claims with nine valid histories and strict core health in 24646 ms. Starting the full Bun gate on identical source."
  "2026-10-20T11:53:09.066Z",codex-agent,"Final bun run release:check passed on identical source commit 7a59afa with isolated HOME/Git configuration and CI=1, under Node 26.12.0 and Bun 1.3.5. Both npm and Bun gates pass 112/112 suite tests and 3/3 packed tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, all 24 authored files at four 100 percent metrics: 1523 statements/lines, 90 functions, 753 branches. Eight-process contention retained all eight distinct claims with nine valid histories and strict core health in 24646 ms (npm) and 28004 ms (Bun). Packed non-Git Node/native Bun installation and full strict health pass. Six behavioral revert proofs are documented. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/pull/10 remains unmerged and unreleased. Existing Git tests and dependency/coverage thresholds are unchanged. Hosted Postgres/MCP acceptance and substantive automated reviews remain unverified; review tools skipped or reported budget limits. Host error titles remain generic, with actionable refusal details. Leaving status in_progress and releasing the claim for owner review."
  "2026-10-20T13:13:32.474Z",codex-agent,"PR #10 review round: fetched all three unresolved threads and all comments; latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range section. All findings verified. Reusing the certified corpus and suppressing unrelated claim reads outside status; guarding foreign sync writes in shared and Git modes; validating empty explicit paths and deduplicating normalized Git paths. Regressions use real trackers and record direct SDK call counts. Branch already contains origin/main; remote head was current. Full npm and Bun release gates and isolated behavioral reverts follow."
  "2026-10-20T13:18:05.178Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs (real isolated source copy, tests import source): restoring only sharedLanes to pre-review code fails 6/6 operation read-budget regressions (extra corpus or claim reads); restoring only SharedTracker.next fails its 1/1 corpus-reuse regression. Restoring only SharedTracker.sync fails the foreign-write regression with Missing expected rejection. Restoring only Swarm.sync fails 3/3 regressions: empty-file rejection, normalized deduplication, and foreign-write protection. Every reverted run exits 1. No dist rebuild needed for source-imported tests. Full-diff self-review found the Git sync ownership instance and direct-SDK whitespace-only paths; both fixed. Production audit has zero vulnerabilities; the existing development-tool advisory is tracked in pm-swarm-zn7m."
  "2026-10-20T13:21:13.773Z",codex-agent,"Final review regressions passed through the pinned pm runner: pm test pm-swarm-shared-tracker --run --only-last --progress, 10/10 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 103147 ms under host load. Test-result tracking is disabled by project configuration, so this comment records the runner result. Re-ran all four isolated function-revert cases against the final test layout; they again fail 6/6, 1/1, 1/1 and 3/3 as expected. Full npm release gate is running with isolated HOME, global/system Git configuration disabled and CI=1; production code and test inputs are fixed for both runtime gates."
  "2026-10-20T13:30:44.402Z",codex-agent,"Npm release gate coverage passed 122/122 tests with zero failures/skips/cancellations. All 24 authored source files are measured; unchanged thresholds pass at 100 percent statements/lines (1526/1526), functions (90/90) and branches (780/780). Identity/privacy, types, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, clean production audit, package dry-run, changelog and release attestation passed. Packed npm/native Bun consumers are running. Eight-process contention retained eight unique claims and nine valid histories with strict core health in 25037 ms."
  "2026-10-20T13:41:04.381Z",codex-agent,"Full npm run release:check passed on the package inputs committed in 856d26a, using isolated HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 and CI=1 with Node 26.12.0/npm 11.20.0. Suite 122/122; packed acceptance 3/3; zero failures/skips/cancellations and no timeout or retry. Four 100 percent dimensions: 1526 statements/lines, 90 functions, 780 branches across 24 authored files. Packed Git npm/npx/native Bun/bunx consumers and the non-Git tarball loop with full strict health pass. Full bun run release:check now starts on identical committed code, tests and package inputs."
  "2026-10-20T13:59:43.017Z",codex-agent,"Full bun run release:check passed on source commit 856d26a with isolated HOME/Git identity and CI=1 under Node 26.12.0 and Bun 1.3.5. Both npm and Bun gates pass 122/122 suite tests and 3/3 packed tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations and no timeout retries. All 24 authored files retain 100 percent: statements/lines 1526/1526, functions 90/90, branches 780/780 (npm) and 781/781 (Bun). Types, identity/privacy, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, clean production audit, package contents, changelog and attestation pass. All 10 new regressions passed via the pinned PM runner. Behavioral function reverts fail as recorded: sharedLanes 6/6, next 1/1, shared sync 1/1, Git sync 3/3. All three threads were valid; no Outside diff range findings existed. The full diff review also fixed Git foreign sync writes and whitespace-only direct SDK paths. Eight-process claim batches took 25037 ms and 16147 ms, retaining eight claims and nine valid histories with strict core health. Packed Node/native Bun non-Git loops pass full strict health without Git. Final handoff changes only PM receipts and verification docs. Existing development-tool advisory remains in pm-swarm-zn7m; hosted coordination remains unverified. No new PM CLI/SDK bugs observed; generic host refusal titles retain actionable details. Leave in_progress and release the claim; do not resolve threads, merge or release."
  "2026-10-20T15:10:28.049Z",codex-agent,"Review round: fetched every review thread and every comment (no pagination remaining). Four unresolved threads: PRRT_kwDOVLY-P86uYd_6, PRRT_kwDOVLY-P86uYeAB, PRRT_kwDOVLY-P86uYeAP, PRRT_kwDOVLY-P86uYeAq. All reproduce in current code; latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Branch contains origin/main. Plan: shared tracker lease outside Git lease, assigned footprint projection, Git ceiling normalization, precise lane documentation; add behavioral regressions and revert proofs, review the entire PR for related defects, then run unchanged npm and Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-20T15:15:12.067Z",codex-agent,"Implemented all four unresolved findings. Git operations now acquire the tracker swarm-operation lease outside the existing repository lease and release both on success/failure. Git overlap checks include assigned-only, SDK-claimed, unknown-footprint and unavailable-local-branch items; terminal and unassigned items do not block. Self-review also fixed own shared-claim conversion by excluding the selected item from its own overlap check, and reused the corpus in Git lane projection. Absolute Git ceilings are normalized while relative entries remain ignored. README, verification documentation and shared lane docstrings now describe assignments accurately. Whole PR diff reviewed across dispatch, selection, watching, packaging, docs and tests; no other valid instance found."
  "2026-10-20T15:15:15.446Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs against pre-round head b1f30c2, in an isolated source copy with real temporary SDK trackers: reverting only Swarm.exclusive makes the lease regression fail 1/1; reverting only Swarm.activeFootprints makes claim, assignment, missing-branch and unknown-footprint regressions fail 4/4; reverting only Swarm.startLane makes own shared-claim conversion fail 1/1; reverting only repositoryRoot makes normalized absolute ceiling regressions fail 3/3; reverting the lane documentation makes the assigned-only documentation/behavior regression fail 1/1. Every revert run exits 1. Source imports require no dist rebuild. Commands: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"Git operations hold\" test/mixed-tracker.test.ts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"Git selection includes shared (claim|assignment|missing-branch|unknown)\" test/mixed-tracker.test.ts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"Git strict start can convert\" test/mixed-tracker.test.ts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"workspace detection normalizes absolute\" test/mixed-tracker.test.ts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"shared assigned-only lanes\" test/mixed-tracker.test.ts. Unmodified new suite passes 14/14, including via pm test --run --only-last --progress; lint/typecheck/duplication pass. A real mixed-mode CLI contention regression is being added before the full release gates."
  "2026-10-20T15:16:12.999Z",codex-agent,"Final focused linked test run passes 15/15 (zero failures, skips or cancellations), including real concurrent Git and non-Git CLI next calls on the same tracker and exactly one retained claim for overlapping work. pm test --run --only-last --progress passed. Build, lint, zero duplication and docstrings pass; fixed an explicit test-array annotation flagged by typecheck before starting release gates. dist is ignored and has no tracked files; npm build regenerates it for packed acceptance. Existing dependency pins, coverage inventory, all four 100 percent thresholds and zero-duplication threshold remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-20T15:24:10.166Z",codex-agent,"Npm release gate suite passed 137/137 with zero failures, skips or cancellations on feab75b. All 24 authored files meet unchanged 100 percent thresholds in every dimension; identity/privacy, typecheck, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, production audit, package dry-run, changelog and release attestation pass. Packed consumer acceptance is running. The eight-process non-Git batch retained all eight claims and nine valid history files with strict core health in 18324 ms. Reconfirmed the previously documented local health boundary: core strict health passes with clean integrity/history and six stale-item advisories; full local health reports the ignored pm-github extension host-version skew (2026.10.15 versus 2026.10.20). No dependency pins or old histories changed."
  "2026-10-20T15:27:47.882Z",codex-agent,"Full npm run release:check PASSED on application code, tests and package inputs in feab75b, with isolated HOME, global/system Git config disabled and CI=true under Node 26.12.0/npm 11.20.0. Suite 137/137; packed acceptance 3/3; zero failures/skips/cancellations and no timeout retries. All 24 authored files meet unchanged 100 percent coverage: statements/lines 1537/1537, functions 90/90, branches 795/795. All other release steps pass, including production audit and zero duplication. Packed Git npm/npx/native Bun/bunx and non-Git Node/native Bun tarball workflows pass. Package dry-run shasum 9f2a515e47f8943ae020c1bafa97ede9d50306ff. Starting the complete Bun release gate on identical code and package inputs."
  "2026-10-20T15:32:16.270Z",codex-agent,"Additional whole-diff ceiling check found a valid adjacent defect after the first npm gate passed: Git resolves ceiling symlinks until an empty entry disables further symlink resolution; lexical absolute normalization alone still throws on a symlinked ceiling. Also canonicalize an existing workspace path to match Git working-directory semantics. Added real-repository regressions for symlink ceilings, the empty-entry sentinel, aliased workspaces, nonexistent ceilings and missing workspace paths. Stopped only the superseded Bun gate to finish this correction; it is not counted as a passing gate. Both full release gates will run again on final code. Earlier npm receipts apply only to feab75b."
  "2026-10-20T15:33:08.053Z",codex-agent,"Additional behavioral revert proof: restore only repositoryRoot from feab75b (the absolute-normalization-only implementation), then run node --test --test-name-pattern=\"workspace detection canonicalizes ceiling symlinks\" test/mixed-tracker.test.ts in an isolated source copy with real Git and SDK trackers. The new symlink/empty-sentinel regression fails 1/1, exit 1, on git rev-parse instead of shared-mode detection. Fixed implementation passes all six ceiling regressions. No dist rebuild needed for source-imported tests. Canonicalization also respects physical workspace paths and ignores nonexistent absolute ceilings. The deliberately stopped earlier Bun run is superseded; final gates will be measured from the next source commit."
  "2026-10-20T15:33:47.671Z",codex-agent,"Final expanded linked regression file passes 17/17 through npx pm test pm-swarm-shared-tracker --run --only-last --progress (zero failures/skips/cancellations). Six targeted ceiling tests, typecheck, lint and zero duplication pass. The new ceiling semantics and source-copy revert proof are documented in docs/shared-tracker-verification.md. Final npm and Bun release gates start after committing this correction; no timeout or retry has been counted as acceptance."
  "2026-10-20T15:49:02.881Z",codex-agent,"FINAL npm release gate PASSED on source commit b3339c3, including the extra symlink ceiling correction. Isolated HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1, CI=true; Node 26.12.0/npm 11.20.0. Suite 139/139; packed acceptance 3/3; zero failures/skips/cancellations and no timeout retries. All 24 authored files retain four unchanged 100 percent thresholds: statements/lines 1546/1546, functions 90/90, branches 802/802. Identity/privacy, typecheck, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, clean production audit, package contents, changelog and attestation pass. Packed Git npm/npx/native Bun/bunx and the non-Git tarball workflow pass. Eight-process batch: eight retained claims, nine valid histories, strict core health, 21903 ms. Package dry-run shasum 0d6760e7519595b4c83b27331f216d770544749d. Starting final Bun gate on identical application code, tests and package inputs."
  "2026-10-20T16:02:22.398Z",codex-agent,"Final Bun gate suite PASSED 139/139 on b3339c3, zero failures/skips/cancellations. All 24 authored sources retain unchanged four 100 percent metrics: statements/lines 1546/1546, functions 90/90, branches 802/802. Audit reports zero production vulnerabilities; zero duplication, identity/privacy, types, lint, docstrings, package contents, changelog and attestation pass. Package shasum matches the final npm gate exactly: 0d6760e7519595b4c83b27331f216d770544749d. Packed consumer acceptance is still running and is not yet counted as passed. Eight-process contention retained eight claims and nine valid histories with strict fixture health in 46153 ms. Remote comparison still reports zero commits behind main."
  "2026-10-20T16:12:12.824Z",codex-agent,"FINAL Bun release gate PASSED on application code, tests and package inputs in b3339c3 under Node 26.12.0 and Bun 1.3.5, with isolated HOME, disabled global/system Git configuration and CI=true. Both final npm and Bun gates pass 139/139 suite tests and 3/3 packed acceptance tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations and no timeout retries. Each measures all 24 authored files at 100 percent: statements/lines 1546/1546, functions 90/90, branches 802/802. Both package hashes match 0d6760e7519595b4c83b27331f216d770544749d. Identity/privacy, typecheck, lint, zero duplication, docstrings, clean production audit, package allowlist, changelog and attestation pass. Packed Git npm/npx/native Bun/bunx and non-Git Node/native Bun workflows pass. Eight-process claim batches retained eight claims and nine valid histories with strict fixture health in 21903 ms (npm) and 46153 ms (Bun). The 17 linked regressions pass. All four threads were valid; no Outside diff range findings existed. Revert proofs fail as required: lease 1/1, footprint projection 4/4, own-claim conversion 1/1, original ceilings 3/3, symlink ceilings 1/1, documentation 1/1; all exit 1. Earlier interrupted Bun run was deliberately superseded for the extra ceiling fix and is not counted. The final receipt commit changes only PM evidence and verification documentation. Existing local extension version skew and stale-item advisories remain separate; hosted coordination is not certified. No new PM CLI/SDK bug was found. Feature remains in progress; release this claim for handoff. No thread response/resolution, merge, tag, release or publication performed."
